.SH "NAME"
pcre2_substring_length_bynumber \- find length of numbered substring
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBint\fP pcre2_substring_length_bynumber(\fBpcre2_match_data\fP *\fImatch_data\fP,
                                    \fBuint32_t\fP \fIstringnumber\fP,
                                    \fBPCRE2_SIZE\fP *\fIsizeptr\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function returns the length of a matched substring, identified by number.
The arguments are:
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 13
\fImatch_data\fP
.ad l
The match data block for the match
.TP 13
\fIstringnumber\fP
.ad l
The substring number
.TP 13
\fIsizeptr\fP
.ad l
Where to return the length, or \f(CRNULL\fP
.PD
.RE
.PP
.ad l
.sp
The third argument may be \f(CRNULL\fP if all you want to know is whether or not a
substring is set. The yield is zero on success, or a negative error code
otherwise. After a partial match, only substring 0 is available.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.